      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, such as 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
